    {
      "id": "18567574261074635",
      "caption": "Acatenango + Fuego + Summit Hike - Sincerity warning: 15 years ago I got sober. It's because of that newfound clarity that I started seeing the world -even when I had no monies. 5 years ago I started experiencing chronic back pain which is so boring to talk about! But most of the time walking out waiting in line was incredibly painful. I started avoiding anything that included those activities (which is a shocking amount). 5 months ago I finally had surgery to fix it. I was pretty scared about it. I'd even cancelled an earlier surgery 2 years prior. I've seen many in recovery get taken out by the isolation and medication that comes after. But thanks to a lot of support from my friends and family I'm ok so far. Naturally, I had to bring this new back out for a test drive. I did what anyone would do and booked a 2 day excursion up a volcano in Guatemala. I'm in recovery because it opens me up to the world -to be awake and willing to do things like this. I'm so so grateful for how lucky I am, for all the help I've had along the way, and for getting my body back. ð¥¹ð",
